The image illustrates a spherical, dendrimer-like nanoparticle, conceptually representing Nano-11 as described in the PDF. It features a highly branched internal structure radiating from a central core, reflecting the high molecular density increasing from the center to the surface, a characteristic of phytoglycogen nanoparticles. This structure contributes to Nano-11's amphiphilic properties and its ability to efficiently adsorb antigens and be taken up by dendritic cells, essential for its role as a vaccine adjuvant.